WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.069
Gon

00:00:02.069 --> 00:00:07.620
What makes Gon such a controversial protagonist?
On the surface Hunter x Hunter, Yoshihiro

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:13.629
Togashi’s long-running magnum opus is a
standard Shounen story. Each story arc focuses

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:19.109
on a well worn Shounen trope such as a training
sequence or a tournament arc, things that

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:25.449
Togashi has covered before in&nbsp;his series
YuYuHakusho. But where&nbsp;Hunter x Hunter&nbsp;fundamentally

00:00:25.449 --> 00:00:30.390
differs from the status quo is in the way
that it takes these formulas and breaks them

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:37.270
apart in interesting ways before returning
to its Shounen roots. In a 2018 interview

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.600
with Weekly Shounen Jump Magazine Togashi
revealed that with Gon he originally planned

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.460
to create a sort of good-boy type of character
that would, and I quote, win every ‘character

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.289
I would want for a son’ competition. But
as soon as he started writing his story, he

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:58.530
immediately realised that this sort of character
would not fit the story he had envisioned

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:05.780
at all. After all, what good boy would lightheartedly
and without so much as a second thought abandon

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:11.060
his foster mother to become a hunter and search
for the father who left him behind as a child

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:17.310
just to follow his own selfish path? And so
it was at that point back in 1998 when the

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:24.070
series published its very first chapter, that
he decided to try something a little bit different.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:28.750
He came to the conclusion that the traditional
tropes of Shounen Manga would not work for

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:33.530
the world he was about to create, and so he
decided to twist the general perspective on

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:40.770
the genre in a number of unimposing, but nonetheless
highly impactful ways. As a result, Gon is

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:47.149
not your classic all-good-all-powerful Shounen
hero, but rather a realistic version of it,

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.670
that has to face real consequences for his
actions within the story world Togashi has

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:56.409
thrown him in. Thus, he has become one of
the most controversially discussed Shounen

00:01:56.409 --> 00:02:01.619
protagonists in history, and in this video
I want to explore with you why I believe that

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:10.150
it makes Gon one of the most well-written
Shounen heroes of all time. //The theme of

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.370
Hunter x Hunter

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.590
Before we can dissect, how Togashi has designed
Gon as a character and what makes his take

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:23.200
on the trope of the Shounen protagonist so
unique, we first have to understand the general

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.390
theme of Hunter x Hunter as a series overall.
You might have heard before that the main

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:33.771
theme of Hunter x Hunter is morality and exploring
the thin lines between good and evil, black

00:02:33.771 --> 00:02:40.400
and white. It’s undeniably true that morality
is a central part of the story’s premise.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.331
However, I believe that the actual theme of
the story goes even further than this. Because

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:52.010
the theme, otherwise also known as the moral
argument of a story, contrary to common believe,

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:57.540
doesn’t refer to a general subject matter
such as love, class, power or good versus

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:04.120
evil. It much rather is the author’s view
on how to act in the world and therefore encompasses

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.560
a certain moral vision, that the author wants
to explore through his story. Therefore, by

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:15.600
definition I believe that morality as a concept
cannot be the overall theme of Hunter x Hunter

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:21.100
but much rather is a part of it. The actual
moral argument that Togashi is exploring in

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:26.640
the story, and that he also uses to explore
Shounen as a genre overall is - ‘What does

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:33.140
it mean to be human in a super-human world?’.
And this overall theme then includes other

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:38.750
important questions, such as ‘what does
it mean to hold power?’ and ultimately also,

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:43.970
‘what does it mean to be moral?’. If you
look closely enough, each character in the

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:49.230
story is a variation of that theme and that’s
exactly what I want to explore with you in

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:53.810
this series of videos, and I hope you enjoy
watching them, as much as I enjoyed making

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.880
them. //Gon &amp; the split hero

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:03.710
So, why start with Gon? Well, Gon is of course
the protagonist of the story. However, Hunter

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:08.410
x Hunter takes a slightly different conceptual
approach to their character web than other

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:15.260
typical Shounen do. No matter if it’s Naruto,
Bleach or One Piece, amidst a usually very

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.090
well-crafted group of supporting main characters,
the hero always stands out clearly as the

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:26.940
central focus point of the story. Therefore,
Naruto is about Naruto himself becoming Hokage.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:32.570
Bleach is about Ichigo following his destiny
as a Shinigami and exploring the supernatural

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:37.840
world. And One Piece is of course about Luffy
striving to find the One Piece and becoming

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:44.590
king of the pirates. But what about Hunter
x Hunter? While Gon does have a central desire

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.710
within his ambition to find his father Ging,
that is driving the story forward, it is neither

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:57.600
particularly intense nor is it very urgent.
The story has no overarching big evil to defeat,

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:03.690
no important object to be acquired and no
final destination to be reached. Rather than

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:08.320
following a straight line towards a major
goal, Gon and his friends follow a meandering

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:14.380
path without apparent direction. They cover
a great deal of territory in a haphazard way

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.930
and encounter a variety of characters from
different levels of society. At the same time

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:24.830
and in close relation to this, in Hunter x
Hunter the lines between protagonist and ally

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:30.470
become very very thin. So thin even, that
it’s fair to say that the story has not

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:38.200
one, but two protagonists - Gon and Killua,
with Gon being only a tad more important.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.640
This trope of the buddy story, is quite common
in Hollywood movies, from stories like the

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:49.100
lord of the rings over 21 Jump street all
the way to pretty much any love story out

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:56.389
there being a typical example. But it is very
very rare in Shounen Anime and Manga. In a

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:02.020
buddy story, in essence, the hero is split
into 2 parts, with one being a bit more relevant

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:07.340
than the other and both main characters having
two different backgrounds, 2 different approaches

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:13.350
to life and 2 different sets of values and
talents. As a result, the whole becomes greater

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:19.050
than the sum of its parts and is what makes
the combination Gon and Killua such a strong

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:24.401
leading duo. These two protagonists are allies
throughout the course of the series, but at

00:06:24.401 --> 00:06:29.490
the same time also have an overarching conflict
of values and actions, that gives character

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:35.120
development to both of them. So, as you can
see Gon is already fundamentally different

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:40.630
from other typical Shounen protagonists, simply
based on his role in the story. His desire

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:45.610
to find his father is not particularly intense
and he shares the role of the hero with his

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:50.950
buddy Killua, who has his very own set of
desires and weaknesses, and we will get further

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:56.480
into their relationship in the next video.
Now this insight, of the split hero, can be

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:02.361
boiled down even further to one of Hunter
x Hunter’s major strengths as a story: While

00:07:02.361 --> 00:07:07.230
many writers believe that all you need is
a well-written hero that is the only person

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:12.380
that matters, Hunter x Hunter doesn’t live
from any individual character, but rather

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:17.770
from an intricately crafted WEB of characters
that interact with each other. As a result,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:23.220
the main group of protagonists move the plot
along, but the don’t carry it all by themselves.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:29.600
And thus, every single character that Togashi
introduces helps to define those around them.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:33.830
So now that we have looked at the general
premise for Gon’s role in the story and

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:39.060
how it differs from conventional Shounen heroes,
let’s finally talk about his character arc.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.750
//Gon Freecss: A dark coming-of-age story

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:47.090
At the beginning of the story, Gon is the
stereotypical shounen poster boy — young,

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:53.310
plucky, irrepressible, spiky hair — in the
first 20 or so episodes, he’s basically

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:59.020
Son Goku without the tail. He is seemingly
nothing but good natured, and depending on

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:03.960
your preferences as viewer his simple and
pure attitude was probably either incredibly

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:10.870
charming or almost intolerable. His main desire
is to find his father Ging and prove himself

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:16.220
in the world of hunters, both of which he
strongly idealises. Equipped with immense

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:21.530
talent, power and skill, he leaves the isolated
island he was raised on to take the hunter

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:28.900
exam and follow his dreams. Togashi makes
us believe that Gon, just as so many other

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:34.060
popular Shounen characters, will grow to become
a warrior of justice, fighting for what is

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:39.030
right. He gives us the impression that in
this story it will be easy to distinguish

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:43.520
who are the good guys and who are the baddies
wearing capes, just as we have been trained

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:49.420
to expect from so many other stories from
that generation. However, it quickly becomes

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:55.160
clear that the world of Hunter x Hunter is
quite cruel and unforgiving. Actions and mistakes

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:01.920
have real consequences here and Togashi basically
used Gon as a sort of literary guinea pig

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.250
to see what would happen to your typical Shounen
Hero, if you were to throw them into a realistic

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:13.500
world. And so slowly but steadily, as we pass
from arc to arc and get to see more and more

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:18.630
of the world and Gon’s interactions with
it, it becomes clearer and clearer that what

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:24.240
now separates Gon from most other Shounen
protagonists is his increasingly skewed moral

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.970
compass.
The fundamental lie that Gon believes about

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:33.470
the world is that everything is either black
or white and that there is a clear line between

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:38.860
good and evil. But since that is not how the
real world works, where morality is mostly

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:44.330
found on a spectrum of grey, Gon increasingly
struggles to define what is good and what

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:51.440
is bad, based on the childish naivety an 11
year old simply has. Since objectively judging

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:56.270
people’s complex actions and behaviour makes
it difficult to put them into one category

00:09:56.270 --> 00:10:02.400
or the other, Gon bases his morality on himself
and his relationship with a person. People

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:08.080
he is familiar with, such as Killua, Leorio
or Kurapika are obviously good and are worthy

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.790
of his protection, while unfamiliar people
dying during the hunter exam are generally

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:19.339
ignored and not considered as important. Meanwhile,
people Gon is unfamiliar with, but that conduct

00:10:19.339 --> 00:10:25.150
acts of violence and cruelty must obviously
be bad. This can strongly be seen when Gon

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:30.080
gets captured by the phantom troupe as he
despises them for taking innocent lives unrelated

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:35.990
to them. At the same time Gon also categories
people based on whether or not they are useful

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:42.170
to him or his friends. Next to his naivety,
this selfishness is Gon’s second major weakness

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:48.580
as a character. As a result his morality appears
to become increasingly skewed, where an objectively

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:54.080
evil and twisted character like Binolt, who
has massacred and eaten countless people,

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:59.600
is actually thanked by Gon simply for helping
him getfing stronger. To better understand

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:04.780
this development in Gon and how his story
ultimately reached the dark climax it did,

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:11.530
I think the best thing is to look at the central
relationship between hero and opponent. //Gon

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.680
&amp; Hisoka

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:20.000
I think it is fair to say that Gon’s relationship
with Hisoka is to Hunter x Hunter what unnecessarily

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:25.620
dramatic music is to this channel. Without
it, it just wouldn’t feel the same. So,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:31.800
when we first get introduced to Hisoka, Togashi
promises us the typical Shounen good-guy-takes-on-bad-guy

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:38.430
relationship between him and Gon. Hisoka is
a psychopathic Clown and the apex of hedonism,

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:43.660
who cuts off another contesters arms simply
for bumping into him right at the start of

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.780
the hunter exam. He will stop at nothing to
get what he wants, no matter the damage it

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:54.150
does to himself or others. As a result, at
the beginning of their relationship Gon and

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:59.899
Hisoka appear to be clear-cut opposites, right
down to Hisoka’s appearance as a scary,

00:11:59.899 --> 00:12:05.890
blood-thirsty clown — which as we know is
the mortal enemy of kids everywhere. Nonetheless,

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:10.620
despite all their seeming differences, over
the course of the story, both characters find

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:15.740
themselves inextricably drawn to each other.
What started off as our typical good-hero

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:22.620
vs evil-opponent dynamic, slowly blurs into
an uncomfortable similarity between the two.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:28.370
Their shared desire to better themselves through
combat and their ecstatic enjoyment of battle

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:34.209
is nothing unique to&nbsp;Hunter x hunter, however
most Shounen tend to shy away from so blatantly

00:12:34.209 --> 00:12:39.110
highlighting this objectively problematic
stance of their main characters. Togashi on

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:44.000
the other hand, makes it easy to imagine a
small misstep in Gon’s life pushing him

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:49.090
into a position similar to Hisoka’s. And
we can see this in the story in a number of

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:55.170
ways. The best example however might be Hisoka’s
fight in the Heaven’s Arena arc against

00:12:55.170 --> 00:13:01.170
the over-confident Kastro. Simply to prove
his superiority and provide a show, Hisoka

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:07.100
sacrifices both his arms to gain the upper
hand (no pun intended), and to satisfy his

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:13.200
desire to dominate and humiliate his opponent.
Then, a little later during the Greed Island

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:19.350
arc, Gon mirrors this morbid sacrifice against
the bomber Genthru. He abandons a carefully

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:24.870
thought out plan by taking an explosive attack
from Genthru which results in him losing an

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:30.970
arm, basically for no other reason but his
desire to prove his superiority and humiliate

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:37.550
his opponent. In a weird way, Gon and Hisoka
become more and more similar throughout the

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:42.990
story to the point where Hisoka almost functions
as a sort of mentor for Gon, a dynamic that

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:48.660
we will explore in more detail in another
video. Now however, we can finally look at

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:54.640
what Gon’s character arc looks like over
all. //Gon’s Character Arc

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:59.310
To summarise what we have discussed so far,
Gon’s character arc shows us what happens

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:05.560
to a naive 11 year old boy that holds enormous
physical power, when he is increasingly confronted

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:11.690
with the harsh &amp; cruel reality of the real
world. This is basically the coming-of-age

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:16.940
story line we know from other Shounen, such
as Naruto, only that Gon doesn’t have a

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:23.550
positive arc, but a negative one. Instead
of growing more emotionally and morally mature,

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:29.450
his character is slowly crushed by the brutal
reality of the Hunter x hunter world. This

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:34.720
twist on the always-rising shounen protagonist,
had not been explored in this much detail

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:40.700
before and has lead to the very mature vibe
hunter x hunter carries as a series. The premise

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:45.720
for Gon’s development throughout the story,
as we have already discussed, are his naivety

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:50.750
and his selfishness. Both of these things
don’t necessarily make him a bad person,

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:56.730
but simply an inexperienced and overwhelmed
child. Nonetheless, based on these weaknesses,

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:02.070
Gon’s character is set up to learn about
the complex moral fabric of society and form

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:07.820
more a realistic view of the world. This need
is also moral, since through his basic moral

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:13.200
compass and his naivety, combined with his
enormous power he starts to hurt people around

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:19.589
him. However, it is not until the chimera
ant arc, that Gon completely spirals into

00:15:19.589 --> 00:15:26.310
a complete loss of his morality and ultimately
his humanity. There are two events in particular

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:31.440
towards the beginning of the arc, that are
representative for this change. The first

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:37.220
is Gon’s first ever kill in the story. A
low-ranked Armadillo chimaera ant that bluntly

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:43.810
attacks him and that Gon then slowly crushes
to death. While it is understandable that

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:49.360
Gon defends himself and maybe even has to
kill the chimera ant, the complete lack of

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:55.060
reaction and emotional response to this act
is what is truly shocking here. The pure Gon

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:59.709
we got to know at the beginning of the story
would never had been able to do such a thing,

00:15:59.709 --> 00:16:06.130
at least without being deeply affected by
it. Yet, Gon has already been so consumed

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:11.510
by power and violence that not only is he
unshaken by his first kill, but doesn’t

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:17.600
even give it a second thought. And even more
impactful, is the death of his mentor Kite,

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:23.660
who is killed by the royal guard Pitou. This
first-ever loss of a loved person affects

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:29.890
Gon deeply, way more than is common for typical
Shounen characters. Much rather Gon has a

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:36.040
very realistic and human response to this
event and develops a rage and thirst for revenge

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:42.100
against Pitou, that is honestly quite unsettling
to watch. As a result, his final act in the

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:47.959
arc is one of the most notorious events in
shonen manga. He uses the heavily injured

00:16:47.959 --> 00:16:53.899
and innocent Komugi as mere a tool to blackmail
Pitou, giving no second thought about the

00:16:53.899 --> 00:16:59.470
overall situation and threatening to kill
her. Once he learns that Kite is beyond help,

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:04.579
in order to satisfy his wrath against Pitou,
he calls upon all of the potential energy

00:17:04.579 --> 00:17:10.419
he will ever have for a short bout of combat
where he brutally kills his opponent without

00:17:10.419 --> 00:17:16.759
a single shred of remorse. In doing so, he
trades the rest of his life for one short

00:17:16.759 --> 00:17:22.579
moment of violence, as the horrified Killua
is unable to do anything but watch. It’s

00:17:22.579 --> 00:17:27.980
some of the most harrowing reading or watching
in the genre, a perverse version of Goku’s

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:34.220
Spirit Bomb. This is Gon’s moment of moral
choice, but instead of having a self-revelation

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:39.820
about what it means to be human and how to
behave justly and morally towards others,

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:46.390
he gives in to his worst instincts. As Killua
abandons his merciless past by forging a relationship

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:52.429
with Gon, his friend sacrifices all of his
remaining humanity for the ultimate act of

00:17:52.429 --> 00:17:58.519
revenge — and becoming a monster in the
process. The self-revelation meant for Gon

00:17:58.519 --> 00:18:05.090
in this moment of extreme moral and human
complexity, is so obvious that we the readers

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:10.580
have it instead and it makes the scene just
the more dark and uncomfortable to watch.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:16.090
The reason, why this dark twist on the typical
Shounen protagonist arc works so well with

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:21.470
Gon, is because Togashi has followed one of
the most important rules of writing when creating

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:29.029
his character: Creating empathy - but not
sympathy. Sympathy means that we approve of

00:18:29.029 --> 00:18:34.289
the heroes actions and completely identify
with him as a person. If that were to be true

00:18:34.289 --> 00:18:39.379
however, we could never have morally challenging
and interesting main characters and every

00:18:39.379 --> 00:18:44.649
single story would only serve a very limited
and specific audience, that shares the exact

00:18:44.649 --> 00:18:49.739
same views and values as the hero. Empathy
on the other hand means that while we don’t

00:18:49.739 --> 00:18:55.571
necessarily approve of the heroes actions,
we do however understand them. We understand

00:18:55.571 --> 00:19:01.100
why the hero would make this decision and
how he ultimately reached that moral conclusion.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:06.139
And as you might suspect, foreshadowing plays
a crucial role in this. It makes the story

00:19:06.139 --> 00:19:12.570
cohesive and engaging. So when we apply this
to Gon, while his brutal murder of Pitou and

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:18.860
his failure to keep his humanity are devastating
to watch, we do fully understand why Gon is

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:23.440
behaving this way and thus feel like we are
watching the natural climax to his character

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:29.960
arc. His entire journey has slowly built towards
this dramatic moment and we could unconsciously

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:36.109
witness Gon’s creeping moral decline, without
Togashi having to throw it into our faces.

00:19:36.109 --> 00:19:42.429
This is truly great writing. It is a great
endpoint to the story, where Gon ultimately

00:19:42.429 --> 00:19:50.169
meets his father and is judged worthy of traveling
with him. He has fulfilled his desire and

00:19:50.169 --> 00:19:56.049
going back to the traditional tropes of shounen,
Togashi establishes a new equilibrium. And

00:19:56.049 --> 00:20:00.669
as the author stated himself, at this point
in Hunter x Hunter - where Gon meets Ging

00:20:00.669 --> 00:20:07.399
- he has pretty much already completed the
story once. Now, you may rightfully say: Doesn’t

00:20:07.399 --> 00:20:12.299
hunter x hunter keep going afterwards? And
of course you’re right. However, as you

00:20:12.299 --> 00:20:17.570
might know if you follow the manga, Gon is
not currently part of the story and should

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:22.029
he ever appear in it again in the form of
a leading character, he will need a completely

00:20:22.029 --> 00:20:28.999
fresh arc with a new desire and now possibly
a positive character arc, where he re-evaluates

00:20:28.999 --> 00:20:35.010
his past actions and ultimately regains his
humanity, ending up better and wiser as at

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:38.619
the beginning of the story.
The one who enabled Gon’s second chance

00:20:38.619 --> 00:20:43.739
and survival meanwhile was his best friend
Killua, who started off as the coldblooded

00:20:43.739 --> 00:20:49.070
and inhuman assassin at the beginning of the
story, who has now completely changed places

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:55.020
with Gon. In many ways Killua is written just
as fantastically as Gon and we will be looking

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:59.960
at his character and role in the story in
the next video of this series. So, stay tuned

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.629
for that. Thanks, guys. Peace.

